---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import portrait from '../assets/artworks/papillons-in-situ.jpg';
---
<Base title="About" nav="about" description="De Sacy is the artist name of Michèle Sacy Chacour, a product designer turned sculptor who transforms steel into layered wall sculptures.">
  <section class="block tint page-top">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <figure class="about-photo"><Image src={portrait} alt="De Sacy beside Le jardin de papillons" widths={[500, 900]} sizes="(max-width: 820px) 100vw, 560px" loading="eager" /></figure>
      <div>
        <span class="label">About the Artist</span>
        <h1 style="margin-block:14px 22px;font-size:clamp(30px,4.4vw,48px);line-height:1.1">Maison De Sacy</h1>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>De Sacy is the artist name of Michèle Sacy Chacour.</p>
          <p>With over 20 years of experience as a product designer specializing in tableware and decorative objects, De Sacy has always been driven by a passion for creating original forms that combine beauty, function, and craftsmanship.</p>
          <p>Her creative journey has now evolved into the world of contemporary art, where she transforms metal into expressive, three-dimensional wall sculptures.</p>
          <p>Through layers, movement, colors, and depth, she creates distinctive pieces that bring walls to life, turning metal into art that tells a story.</p>
          <p>De Sacy lives and works in Beirut, Lebanon.</p>
        </div>
        <blockquote class="statement">
          <p>My work is about capturing the energy of speed and holding it still. After twenty years of designing objects to be used, I now focus on creating sculptures to be experienced, where the strength of steel meets the raw rush of human motion.</p>
          <p>I don't see steel as a cold or heavy material; I see it as a way to trap the thrill of a split second.</p>
          <footer>Artist statement</footer>
        </blockquote>
        <div class="pair">
          <div><b>Artwork</b>Sculpture as a work of art. Unique pieces and limited editions, with a certificate of authenticity.</div>
          <div><b>Studio</b>Personal pieces, 20 to 80 cm, made to order.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
